  "body": "Currently, a [lock](https://fs.spec.whatwg.org/#file-entry-lock) may only be taken on a file entry. This should be extended to support locking directories, too.\r\n\r\nThis is one of the [proposed changes](https://github.com/whatwg/fs/blob/main/proposals/MultipleReadersWriters.md#preventing-modification-of-parents) to support #34, but it's also needed to properly support operations which modify a directory (such as `remove()` #9, `removeEntry()`, and `move()` #10 of directories)\r\n\r\nOperations which modify a directory should require taking an exclusive lock on the directory, which should only succeed if no contained file is locked",
